      "message": "The `aom_memset16()` function prototype is modeled after that of [`memset()`](https://en.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/memset), which declares its second parameter as `int`:\n\n```\nvoid* memset( void* dest, int ch, size_t count );\n```\n\nI am sure it is possible to handle this properly inside `aom_memset16()`. Could you please try adding a `uint16_t` cast to `aom_memset16()` as follows?\n\n```\nstatic inline void *aom_memset16(void *dest, int val, size_t length) {\n  size_t i;\n  uint16_t *dest16 \u003d (uint16_t *)dest;\n  for (i \u003d 0; i \u003c length; i++) *dest16++ \u003d (uint16_t)val;    \u003c\u003d NOTE THE CAST\n  return dest;\n}\n```",
